        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A rare fast-flow vascular anomaly characterized by direct extracranial artery-to-vein communication without an intervening nidus. The majority of the cases are asymptomatic. When present the symptoms may include fatigue dyspnea palpitations congestive heart failure and pulmonary hypertension."
